{
  "_comment": "Comment-line CEILING per file, one entry per tracked file under src/, scripts/, deploy/, .github/workflows/, bin/ and hooks/. Measured and enforced by scripts/comment-load-ratchet.mjs; the standard it holds the volume half of is docs/comment-standard.md. A recorded number is a ceiling on ONE file, not a target: today's count is legal forever. The script rewrites an entry DOWN when a file shrinks, records a new file, and drops a deleted one -- all without review. Only RAISING an entry is refused, and the only way to raise one is this edit, which a reviewer reads: that visibility is the whole point. Never raise an entry to silence a red PR without first asking whether the prose belongs in learnings/*.yaml or a dated docs/ page instead. Captured 2026-09-05 from main at ea02cc83 plus this PR's own new files. HOW GROWTH IS JUDGED (corrected 2026-09-05, after this gate reddened its own PR three times in forty minutes): a file over its recorded number is re-read AT THE MERGE BASE, and refused only if it is longer than it already was there. CI measures the MERGE ref, so a ledger captured at one moment goes short every time main lands a comment, and without the base check the gate refuses PRs that changed nothing. Inherited growth is recorded here automatically; growth a diff actually added is refused and must be shortened or recorded deliberately. Residual cost, the one scripts/source-size-baseline.json already documents: two concurrent PRs that both grow the SAME file edit the same line here and conflict. If that becomes common the fix is that file's bucket trick (CEILING_BUCKET_LINES), not a wider gate.",
